ed straight line and the square on the added straight line both together are double the sum of the square on the half and the square described on the straight line made up of the half and the added straight line as on one straight line.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.11", "PropI.3", "PropI.31", "PropI.29", "PostI.1", "PropI.5", "PropI.32", "PropI.15", "PropI.6", "PropI.34", "PropI.47" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropII.11" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 11, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.11.md", "Statement" -> "To cut a given straight line so that the rectangle contained by the whole and one of the segments equals the square on the remaining segment.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropI.10", "PropI.3", "PropII.6", "PropI.47" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIV.10", "PropXIII.17" } |>, "PropII.12" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 12, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.12.md", "Statement" -> "In obtuse-angled triangles the square on the side opposite the obtuse angle is greater than the sum of the squares on the sides containing the obtuse angle by twice the rectangle contained by one of the sides about the obtuse angle, namely that on which the perpendicular falls, and the straight line cut off outside by the perpendicular towards the obtuse angle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.12", "PropII.4", "PropI.47" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropII.13" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 13, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.13.md", "Statement" -> "In acute-angled triangles the square on the side opposite the acute angle is less than the sum of the squares on the sides containing the acute angle by twice the rectangle contained by one of the sides about the acute angle, namely that on which the perpendicular falls, and the straight line cut off within by the perpendicular towards the acute angle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.12", "PropII.7", "PropI.47" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropII.14" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 14, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.14.md", "Statement" -> "To construct a square equal to a given rectilinear figure.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.45", "PropI.3", "PropI.10", "DefI.15", "PropII.5", "PropI.47" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropII.2" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 2, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.2.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is cut at random, then the sum of the rectangles contained by the whole and each of the segments equals the square on the whole.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropI.31" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropXIII.10" } |>, "PropII.3" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 3, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.3.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is cut at random, then the rectangle contained by the whole and one of the segments equals the sum of the rectangle contained by the segments and the square on the aforesaid segment.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropI.31" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.15" } |>, "PropII.4" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 4, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.4.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is cut at random, then the square on the whole equals the sum of the squares on the segments plus twice the rectangle contained by the segments.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropI.31", "PropI.29", "PropI.5", "PropI.6", "PropI.34", "PropI.43" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropII.12", "PropIX.15", "PropX.26", "PropX.36", "PropX.37", "PropX.38", "PropX.42", "PropX.44", "PropX.47", "PropX.54" } |>, "PropII.5" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 5, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.5.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is cut into equal and unequal segments, then the rectangle contained by the unequal segments of the whole together with the square on the straight line between the points of section equals the square on the half.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropI.31", "PropI.43", "PropI.36" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropII.14", "PropIII.35", "PropX.17" } |>, "PropII.6" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 6, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.6.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is bisected and a straight line is added to it in a straight line, then the rectangle contained by the whole with the added straight line and the added straight line together with the square on the half equals the square on the straight line made up of the half and the added straight line.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropI.31", "PropI.36", "PropI.43" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropII.11", "PropIII.36" } |>, "PropII.7" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 7, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.7.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is cut at random, then the sum of the square on the whole and that on one of the segments equals twice the rectangle contained by the whole and the said segment plus the square on the remaining segment.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropI.31", "PropI.43" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropII.13", "PropX.100", "PropX.101", "PropX.102", "PropX.73", "PropX.74", "PropX.75", "PropX.76", "PropX.77", "PropX.78", "PropX.79", "PropX.80", "PropX.81", "PropX.84", "PropX.97", "PropX.98", "PropX.99" } |>, "PropII.8" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 8, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.8.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is cut at random, then four times the rectangle contained by the whole and one of the segments plus the square on the remaining segment equals the square described on the whole and the aforesaid segment as on one straight line.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.3", "PropI.46", "PropI.31", "PropI.34", "PropI.36", "PropI.43" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropII.9" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "II", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 9, "File" -> "Wiki/BookII/PropII.9.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is cut into equal and unequal segments, then the sum of the squares on the unequal segments of the whole is double the sum of the square on the half and the square on the straight line between the points of section.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.11", "PropI.3", "PropI.31", "PropI.5", "PropI.32", "PropI.29", "PropI.6", "PropI.47", "PropI.34" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.1" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 1, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.1.md", "Statement" -> "*Equal circles* are those whose diameters are equal, or whose radii are equal.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.10" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 10, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.10.md", "Statement" -> "A *sector* of a circle is the figure which, when an angle is constructed at the center of the circle, is contained by the straight lines containing the angle and the circumference cut off by them.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.11" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 11, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.11.md", "Statement" -> "Similar segments of circles are those which admit equal angles, or in which the angles equal one another.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.23", "PropIII.26" } |>, "DefIII.2" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 2, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.2.md", "Statement" -> "A straight line is said to *touch* a circle which, meeting the circle and being produced, does not cut the circle.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.13" } |>, "DefIII.3" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 3, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.3.md", "Statement" -> "Circles are said to *touch* one another which meet one another but do not cut one another.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.4" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 4, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.4.md", "Statement" -> "Straight lines in a circle are said to be *equally distant* from the center when the perpendiculars drawn to them from the center are equal.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.14", "PropIII.15" } |>, "DefIII.5" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 5, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.5.md", "Statement" -> "And that straight line is said to be at a *greater distance* on which the greater perpendicular falls.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.6" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 6, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.6.md", "Statement" -> "A *segment* of a circle is the figure contained by a straight line and a circumference of a circle.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.7" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 7, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.7.md", "Statement" -> "An *angle of a segment* is that contained by a straight line and a circumference of a circle.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.8" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 8, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.8.md", "Statement" -> "An *angle in a segment* is the angle which, when a point is taken on the circumference of the segment and straight lines are joined from it to the ends of the straight line which is the base of the segment, is contained by the straight lines so joined.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefIII.9" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 9, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/DefIII.9.md", "Statement" -> "And, when the straight lines containing the angle cut off a circumference, the angle is said to *stand upon* that circumference.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIII.1" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 1, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.1.md", "Statement" -> "To find the center of a given circle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.10", "PropI.11", "DefI.15", "PropI.8", "DefI.10" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.10", "PropIII.11", "PropIII.12", "PropIII.13", "PropIII.14", "PropIII.17", "PropIII.18", "PropIII.2", "PropIII.21", "PropIII.28", "PropIII.29", "PropIII.3", "PropIII.35", "PropIII.36", "PropIII.37", "PropIII.4", "PropIII.8", "PropIII.9", "PropIV.12", "PropIV.15", "PropIV.3", "PropIV.6", "PropIV.7", "PropXI.23", "PropXIII.10", "PropXIII.11", "PropXIII.12", "PropXIII.16", "PropXIII.9" } |>, "PropIII.10" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 10, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.10.md", "Statement" -> "A circle does not cut a circle at more than two points.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.10", "PropI.11", "PropIII.1", "PropIII.5" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.24" } |>, "PropIII.11" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 11, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.11.md", "Statement" -> "If two circles touch one another internally, and their centers are taken, then the straight line joining their centers, being produced, falls on the point of contact of the circles.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "PropI.20" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.13" } |>, "PropIII.12" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 12, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.12.md", "Statement" -> "If two circles touch one another externally, then the straight line joining their centers passes through the point of contact.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "PropI.20" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIII.13" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 13, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.13.md", "Statement" -> "A circle does not touch another circle at more than one point whether it touches it internally or externally.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "PropIII.11", "PropIII.2", "DefIII.2" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIII.14" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 14, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.14.md", "Statement" -> "Equal straight lines in a circle are equally distant from the center, and those which are equally distant from the center equal one another.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "PropI.12", "PropIII.3", "PropI.47", "DefIII.4" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.15" } |>, "PropIII.15" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 15, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.15.md", "Statement" -> "Of straight lines in a circle the diameter is greatest, and of the rest the nearer to the center is always greater than the more remote.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.12", "DefIII.4", "PropI.3", "PropI.11", "PropIII.14", "PropI.20", "PropI.24" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIII.16" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 16, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.16.md", "Statement" -> "The straight line drawn at right angles to the diameter of a circle from its end will fall outside the circle, and into the space between the straight line and the circumference another straight line cannot be interposed, further the angle of the semicircle is greater, and the remaining angle less, than any acute rectilinear angle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.5", "PropI.17", "PropI.12", "PropI.19" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.17", "PropIII.33", "PropIII.37", "PropIV.12", "PropIV.13", "PropIV.2", "PropIV.3", "PropIV.4", "PropIV.7", "PropXII.16" } |>, "PropIII.17" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 17, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.17.md", "Statement" -> "From a given point to draw a straight line touching a given circle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "PropI.11", "PropI.4", "PropIII.16" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.34", "PropIII.37", "PropXII.2" } |>, "PropIII.18" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 18, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.18.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line touches a circle, and a straight line is joined from the center to the point of contact, the straight line so joined will be perpendicular to the tangent.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "PropI.12", "PropI.17", "PropI.19" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.19", "PropIII.36", "PropIII.37", "PropIV.12", "PropIV.3", "PropIV.7" } |>, "PropIII.19" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 19, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.19.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line touches a circle, and from the point of contact a straight line is drawn at right angles to the tangent, the center of the circle will be on the straight line so drawn.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.11", "PropIII.18" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.32" } |>, "PropIII.2" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 2, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.2.md", "Statement" -> "If two points are taken at random on the circumference of a circle, then the straight line joining the points falls within the circle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "DefI.15", "PropI.5", "PropI.16", "PropI.19" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.13" } |>, "PropIII.20" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 20, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.20.md", "Statement" -> "In a circle the angle at the center is double the angle at the circumference when the angles have the same circumference as base.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.5", "PropI.32" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.21", "PropIII.27", "PropVI.33" } |>, "PropIII.21" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 21, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.21.md", "Statement" -> "In a circle the angles in the same segment equal one another.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.1", "PropIII.20" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.22" } |>, "PropIII.22" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 22, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.22.md", "Statement" -> "The sum of the opposite angles of quadrilaterals in circles equals two right angles.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.32", "PropIII.21" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.31", "PropIII.32" } |>, "PropIII.23" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 23, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.23.md", "Statement" -> "On the same straight line there cannot be constructed two similar and unequal segments of circles on the same side.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefIII.11", "PropI.16" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.24" } |>, "PropIII.24" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 24, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.24.md", "Statement" -> "Similar segments of circles on equal straight lines equal one another.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.23", "PropIII.10", "CNI.1" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.26" } |>, "PropIII.25" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 25, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.25.md", "Statement" -> "Given a segment of a circle, to describe the complete circle of which it is a segment.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.10", "PropI.11", "PropI.23", "PropI.6", "PropI.4", "PropIII.9" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIII.26" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 26, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.26.md", "Statement" -> "In equal circles equal angles stand on equal circumferences whether they stand at the centers or at the circumferences.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.4", "DefIII.11", "PropIII.24" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.28", "PropIV.11", "PropIV.15", "PropXIII.10" } |>, "PropIII.27" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 27, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.27.md", "Statement" -> "In equal circles angles standing on equal circumferences equal one another whether they stand at the centers or at the circumferences.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.23", "PropI.26", "PropIII.20" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIII.29", "PropIV.11", "PropIV.12", "PropIV.15", "PropVI.33", "PropXII.1", "PropXII.17" } |>, "PropIII.28" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "III", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 28, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIII/PropIII.28.md", "Statement" -> "In equal circles equal straight lines cut off equal circumferences, the