-> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.15.md", "Statement" -> "In equal triangles which have one angle equal to one angle the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional; and those triangles which have one angle equal to one angle, and in which the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional, are equal.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.14", "PropV.7", "PropVI.1", "PropV.11", "PropV.9" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.19" } |>, "PropVI.16" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 16, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.16.md", "Statement" -> "If four straight lines are proportional, then the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means; and, if the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means, then the four straight lines are proportional.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.11", "PropI.3", "PropI.31", "PropV.7", "PropVI.14" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.17", "PropX.112", "PropX.113", "PropX.28" } |>, "PropVI.17" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 17, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.17.md", "Statement" -> "If three straight lines are proportional, then the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the square on the mean; and, if the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the square on the mean, then the three straight lines are proportional.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.3", "PropV.7", "PropV.11", "PropVI.16" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropX.100", "PropX.25", "PropX.27", "PropX.28", "PropX.54", "PropX.60", "PropX.91", "PropX.92", "PropX.93", "PropX.94", "PropX.97", "PropX.98", "PropXIII.1", "PropXIII.10", "PropXIII.13", "PropXIII.4", "PropXIII.5", "PropXIII.6" } |>, "PropVI.18" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 18, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.18.md", "Statement" -> "To describe a rectilinear figure similar and similarly situated to a given rectilinear figure on a given straight line.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.23", "PropI.32", "PropVI.4", "PropV.16", "PropV.11", "DefVI.1" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.22", "PropVI.25", "PropVI.28" } |>, "PropVI.19" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 19, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.19.md", "Statement" -> "Similar triangles are to one another in the duplicate ratio of the corresponding sides.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefV.11", "PropVI.11", "PropV.16", "PropV.11", "PropVI.15", "DefV.8", "PropVI.1", "PropV.7" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.20", "PropVI.22", "PropVI.31" } |>, "PropVI.2" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 2, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.2.md", "Statement" -> "If a straight line is drawn parallel to one of the sides of a triangle, then it cuts the sides of the triangle proportionally; and, if the sides of the triangle are cut proportionally, then the line joining the points of section is parallel to the remaining side of the triangle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.37", "PropV.7", "PropVI.1", "PropV.11", "PropV.9", "PropI.39" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.10", "PropVI.11", "PropVI.12", "PropVI.24", "PropVI.3", "PropVI.4", "PropVI.9", "PropXI.17", "PropXI.23", "PropXII.17", "PropXII.3" } |>, "PropVI.20" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 20, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.20.md", "Statement" -> "Similar polygons are divided into similar triangles, and into triangles equal in multitude and in the same ratio as the wholes, and the polygon has to the polygon a ratio duplicate of that which the corresponding side has to the corresponding side.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVI.1", "PropVI.6", "PropVI.4", "PropV.22", "PropI.32", "PropVI.1", "PropV.12", "PropV.11", "PropV.16", "PropVI.19" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropX.68", "PropX.9", "PropXII.1" } |>, "PropVI.21" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 21, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.21.md", "Statement" -> "Figures which are similar to the same rectilinear figure are also similar to one another.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVI.1", "PropV.11" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.24", "PropVI.28", "PropVI.29" } |>, "PropVI.22" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 22, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.22.md", "Statement" -> "If four straight lines are proportional, then the rectilinear figures similar and similarly described upon them are also proportional; and, if the rectilinear figures similar and similarly described upon them are proportional, then the straight lines are themselves also proportional.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVI.11", "PropV.11", "PropV.22", "PropVI.19", "PropVI.12", "PropVI.18", "PropV.9" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropX.105", "PropX.112", "PropX.14", "PropX.22", "PropXII.4" } |>, "PropVI.23" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 23, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.23.md", "Statement" -> "Equiangular parallelograms have to one another the ratio compounded of the ratios of their sides.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.14", "PropI.31", "PropVI.12", "PropVI.1", "PropV.11", "PropV.22" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropVI.24" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 24, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.24.md", "Statement" -> "In any parallelogram the parallelograms about the diameter are similar both to the whole and to one another.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVI.2", "PropV.18", "PropV.16", "PropI.29", "PropV.22", "DefVI.1", "PropVI.21" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.26", "PropVI.29" } |>, "PropVI.25" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 25, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.25.md", "Statement" -> "To construct a figure similar to one given rectilinear figure and equal to another.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.44", "PropI.45", "PropVI.13", "PropVI.18", "PropV.19", "PropVI.1", "PropV.11", "PropV.16", "DefV.5" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.28", "PropVI.29" } |>, "PropVI.26" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 26, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.26.md", "Statement" -> "If from a parallelogram there is taken away a parallelogram similar and similarly situated to the whole and having a common angle with it, then it is about the same diameter with the whole.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.31", "PropVI.24", "DefVI.1", "PropV.11", "PropV.9" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.27", "PropVI.28", "PropVI.29", "PropX.91", "PropX.92", "PropX.93", "PropX.94", "PropX.95", "PropX.96" } |>, "PropVI.27" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 27, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.27.md", "Statement" -> "Of all the parallelograms applied to the same straight line falling short by parallelogrammic figures similar and similarly situated to that described on the half of the straight line, that parallelogram is greatest which is applied to the half of the straight line and is similar to the difference.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVI.26", "PropI.43", "PropI.36" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.28" } |>, "PropVI.28" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 28, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.28.md", "Statement" -> "To apply a parallelogram equal to a given rectilinear figure to a given straight line but falling short by a parallelogram similar to a given one; thus the given rectilinear figure must not be greater than the parallelogram described on the half of the straight line and similar to the given parallelogram.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVI.27", "PropI.9", "PropVI.18", "PropVI.25", "PropVI.21", "PropVI.26", "PropI.36" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropX.33", "PropX.34" } |>, "PropVI.29" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 29, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.29.md", "Statement" -> "To apply a parallelogram equal to a given rectilinear figure to a given straight line but exceeding it by a parallelogram similar to a given one.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVI.25", "PropVI.21", "PropVI.26", "PropI.36", "PropI.43", "PropVI.24" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.30" } |>, "PropVI.3" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 3, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.3.md", "Statement" -> "If an angle of a triangle is bisected by a straight line cutting the base, then the segments of the base have the same ratio as the remaining sides of the triangle; and, if segments of the base have the same ratio as the remaining sides of the triangle, then the straight line joining the vertex to the point of section bisects the angle of the triangle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.31", "PropI.29", "PropI.6", "PropVI.2", "PropV.7", "PropV.11", "PropV.9", "PropI.5" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropVI.30" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 30, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.30.md", "Statement" -> "To cut a given finite straight line in extreme and mean ratio.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.46", "PropVI.29", "PropV.7", "DefVI.3", "PropVI.14" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropXIII.17" } |>, "PropVI.31" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 31, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.31.md", "Statement" -> "In right-angled triangles the figure on the side opposite the right angle equals the sum of the similar and similarly described figures on the sides containing the right angle.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.12", "PropVI.8", "DefVI.1", "PropVI.19", "PropV.24" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropVI.32" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 32, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.32.md", "Statement" -> "If two triangles having two sides proportional to two sides are placed together at one angle so that their corresponding sides are also parallel, then the remaining sides of the triangles are in a straight line.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.29", "PropVI.6", "PropI.32", "PropI.14" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropXIII.17" } |>, "PropVI.33" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 33, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.33.md", "Statement" -> "Angles in equal circles have the same ratio as the circumferences on which they stand whether they stand at the centers or at the circumferences.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIII.27", "DefV.5", "PropV.15", "PropIII.20" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropXIII.10", "PropXIII.8", "PropXIII.9" } |>, "PropVI.4" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 4, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.4.md", "Statement" -> "In equiangular triangles the sides about the equal angles are proportional where the corresponding sides are opposite the equal angles.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.17", "PostI.1", "PropI.28", "PropI.34", "PropVI.2", "PropV.7", "PropV.16", "PropV.22" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.18", "PropVI.20", "PropVI.5", "PropVI.6", "PropVI.7", "PropVI.8", "PropXI.23", "PropXI.36", "PropXII.1", "PropXIII.10", "PropXIII.18", "PropXIII.8", "PropXIII.9" } |>, "PropVI.5" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 5, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.5.md", "Statement" -> "If two triangles have their sides proportional, then the triangles are equiangular with the equal angles opposite the corresponding sides.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.23", "PropI.32", "PropVI.4", "PropV.11", "PropV.9", "PropI.8", "PropI.4" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropXII.12" } |>, "PropVI.6" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 6, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.6.md", "Statement" -> "If two triangles have one angle equal to one angle and the sides about the equal angles proportional, then the triangles are equiangular and have those angles equal opposite the corresponding sides.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.23", "PropI.32", "PropVI.4", "PropV.11", "PropV.9", "PropI.4" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.20", "PropVI.32", "PropXII.1", "PropXII.12" } |>, "PropVI.7" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 7, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.7.md", "Statement" -> "If two triangles have one angle equal to one angle, the sides about other angles proportional, and the remaining angles either both less or both not less than a right angle, then the triangles are equiangular and have those angles equal the sides about which are proportional.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.23", "PropI.32", "PropVI.4", "PropV.11", "PropV.9", "PropI.5", "PropI.13", "PropI.17" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropVI.8" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 8, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.8.md", "Statement" -> "If in a right-angled triangle a perpendicular is drawn from the right angle to the base, then the triangles adjoining the perpendicular are similar both to the whole and to one another.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.32", "PropVI.4", "DefVI.1" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVI.13", "PropVI.31", "PropXII.17", "PropXIII.13", "PropXIII.16", "PropXIII.18" } |>, "PropVI.9" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VI", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 9, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVI/PropVI.9.md", "Statement" -> "To cut off a prescribed part from a given straight line.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropI.3", "PropI.31", "PropVI.2" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropXIII.11", "PropXIII.13", "PropXIII.15", "PropXIII.16" } |>, "DefVII.1" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 1, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.1.md", "Statement" -> "A *unit* is that by virtue of which each of the things that exist is called one.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.7" } |>, "DefVII.10" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 10, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.10.md", "Statement" -> "An *odd-times-odd number* is that which is measured by an odd number according to an odd number.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.11" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 11, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.11.md", "Statement" -> "A *prime number* is that which is measured by a unit alone.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.12", "PropIX.7", "PropVII.1", "PropVII.2", "PropVII.21", "PropVII.23", "PropVII.24", "PropVII.28", "PropVII.29", "PropVII.31" } |>, "DefVII.12" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 12, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.12.md", "Statement" -> "Numbers *relatively prime* are those which are measured by a unit alone as a common measure.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.13" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 13, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.13.md", "Statement" -> "A *composite number* is that which is measured by some number.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.14" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 14, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.14.md", "Statement" -> "Numbers *relatively composite* are those which are measured by some number as a common measure.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.15" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 15, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.15.md", "Statement" -> "A number is said to *multiply* a number when the latter is added as many times as there are units in the former.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.28", "PropIX.29", "PropIX.7", "PropVII.16", "PropVII.17", "PropVII.22", "PropVII.24", "PropVII.30", "PropVII.33", "PropVII.34" } |>, "DefVII.16" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 16, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.16.md", "Statement" -> "And, when two numbers having multiplied one another make some number, the number so produced be called *plane,* and its *sides* are the numbers which have multiplied one another.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.17" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 17, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.17.md", "Statement" -> "And, when three numbers having multiplied one another make some number, the number so produced be called *solid,* and its *sides* are the numbers which have multiplied one another.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.18" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 18, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.18.md", "Statement" -> "A *square number* is equal multiplied by equal, or a number which is contained by two equal numbers.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.19" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 19, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.19.md", "Statement" -> "And a *cube* is equal multiplied by equal and again by equal, or a number which is contained by three equal numbers.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.2" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 2, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.2.md", "Statement" -> "A *number* is a multitude composed of units.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.20" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 20, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.20.md", "Statement" -> "Numbers are *proportional* when the first is the same multiple, or the same part, or the same parts, of the second that the third is of the fourth.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.3", "PropIX.36", "PropIX.6", "PropIX.8", "PropVII.11", "PropVII.12", "PropVII.13", "PropVII.15", "PropVII.17", "PropVII.20", "PropVII.33", "PropVIII.10", "PropVIII.14", "PropVIII.15", "PropVIII.4", "PropVIII.6", "PropVIII.8", "PropVIII.9", "PropX.5", "PropX.6" } |>, "DefVII.21" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 21, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.21.md", "Statement" -> "*Similar plane* and *solid* numbers are those which have their sides proportional.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVIII.18", "PropVIII.19" } |>, "DefVII.22" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 22, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.22.md", "Statement" -> "A *perfect number* is that which is equal to the sum of its own parts.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.36" } |>, "DefVII.3" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 3, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.3.md", "Statement" -> "A number is *a part* of a number, the less of the greater, when it measures the greater;", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVII.4" } |>, "DefVII.4" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 4, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.4.md", "Statement" -> "But *parts* when it does not measure it.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.5" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 5, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.5.md", "Statement" -> "The greater number is a *multiple* of the less when it is measured by the less.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.6" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 6, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.6.md", "Statement" -> "An *even number* is that which is divisible into two equal parts.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.21", "PropIX.22", "PropIX.23", "PropIX.24", "PropIX.25", "PropIX.26", "PropIX.27", "PropIX.32", "PropIX.33", "PropIX.34" } |>, "DefVII.7" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 7, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.7.md", "Statement" -> "An *odd number* is that which is not divisible into two equal parts, or that which differs by a unit from an even number.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.8" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 8, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.8.md", "Statement" -> "An *even-times-even number* is that which is measured by an even number according to an even number.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefVII.9" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 9, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/DefVII.9.md", "Statement" -> "An *even-times-odd number* is that which is measured by an even number according to an odd number.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropVII.1" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 1, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.1.md", "Statement" -> "When two unequal numbers are set out, and the less is continually subtracted in turn from the greater, if the number which is left never measures the one before it until a unit is left, then the original numbers are relatively prime.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.11" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVII.2" } |>, "PropVII.10" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 10, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.10.md", "Statement" -> "If a number is parts of a number, and another is the same parts of another, then alternately, whatever part of parts the first is of the third, the same part, or the same parts, the second is of the fourth.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.9", "PropVII.5", "PropVII.6" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVII.13" } |>, "PropVII.11" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 11, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.11.md", "Statement" -> "If a whole is to a whole as a subtracted number is to a subtracted number, then the remainder is to the remainder as the whole is to the whole.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.20", "PropVII.7", "PropVII.8" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.35" } |>, "PropVII.12" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 12, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.12.md", "Statement" -> "If any number of numbers are proportional, then one of the antecedents is to one of the consequents as the sum of the antecedents is to the sum of the consequents.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.20", "PropVII.5", "PropVII.6" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.35", "PropVII.15", "PropVII.20" } |>, "PropVII.13" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 13, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.13.md", "Statement" -> "If four numbers are proportional, then they are also proportional alternately.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.20", "PropVII.10" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.17", "PropIX.35", "PropVII.14", "PropVII.17", "PropVII.20", "PropVIII.18", "PropVIII.19", "PropVIII.20", "PropVIII.4" } |>, "PropVII.14" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 14, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.14.md", "Statement" -> "If there are any number of numbers, and others equal to them in multitude, which taken two and two together are in the same ratio, then they are also in the same ratio *ex aequali.*", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.13", "PropV.11" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.36", "PropVIII.1", "PropVIII.13", "PropVIII.21", "PropVIII.5", "PropVIII.6", "PropVIII.8" } |>, "PropVII.15" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 15, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.15.md", "Statement" -> "If a unit measures any number, and another number measures any other number the same number of times, then alternately, the unit measures the third number the same number of times that the second measures the fourth.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.12", "DefVII.20" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.11", "PropVII.16", "PropVII.37", "PropVII.38" } |>, "PropVII.16" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 16, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.16.md", "Statement" -> "If two numbers multiplied by one another make certain numbers, then the numbers so produced equal one another.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.15", "PropVII.15" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVII.18", "PropVII.21", "PropVII.24", "PropVII.33" } |>, "PropVII.17" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 17, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.17.md", "Statement" -> "If a number multiplied by two numbers makes certain numbers, then the numbers so produced have the same ratio as the numbers multiplied.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.15", "DefVII.20", "PropV.11", "PropVII.13" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.1", "PropIX.2", "PropIX.4", "PropIX.5", "PropVII.18", "PropVII.19", "PropVII.22", "PropVII.34", "PropVIII.10", "PropVIII.11", "PropVIII.12", "PropVIII.18", "PropVIII.19", "PropVIII.2", "PropVIII.20", "PropVIII.5" } |>, "PropVII.18" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 18, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.18.md", "Statement" -> "If two numbers multiplied by any number make certain numbers, then the numbers so produced have the same ratio as the multipliers.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.16", "PropVII.17" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVII.19", "PropVII.34", "PropVIII.10", "PropVIII.11", "PropVIII.12", "PropVIII.19", "PropVIII.2", "PropVIII.21" } |>, "PropVII.19" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 19, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.19.md", "Statement" -> "If four numbers are proportional, then the number produced from the first and fourth equals the number produced from the second and third; and, if the number produced from the first and fourth equals that produced from the second and third, then the four numbers are proportional.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.17", "PropV.11", "PropVII.18", "PropV.9", "PropV.7" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.12", "PropIX.13", "PropIX.18", "PropIX.36", "PropVII.24", "PropVII.30", "PropVII.33", "PropVII.34" } |>, "PropVII.2" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 2, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.2.md", "Statement" -> "To find the greatest common measure of two given numbers not relatively prime.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.11", "PropVII.1" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropVII.3", "PropVII.4" } |>, "PropVII.20" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 20, "File" -> "Wiki/BookVII/PropVII.20.md", "Statement" -> "The least numbers of those which have the same ratio with them measure those which have the same ratio with them the same number of times; the greater the greater; and the less the less.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.13", "DefVII.20", "PropVII.12", "PropVII.4" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.12", "PropIX.16", "PropIX.17", "PropIX.36", "PropVII.21", "PropVII.24", "PropVII.30", "PropVII.34", "PropVIII.1", "PropVIII.20", "PropVIII.21", "PropVIII.4", "PropVIII.8" } |>, "PropVII.21" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "VII", "Group" -> Null, 