ultiplied by an even number, then the product is even.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.15", "PropIX.21" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.31" } |>, "PropIX.29" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 29, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.29.md", "Statement" -> "If an odd number is multiplied by an odd number, then the product is odd.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.15", "PropIX.23" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.3" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 3, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.3.md", "Statement" -> "If a cubic number multiplied by itself makes some number, then the product is a cube.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.20", "PropVIII.8", "PropVIII.23" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.4", "PropIX.5", "PropIX.9" } |>, "PropIX.30" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 30, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.30.md", "Statement" -> "If an odd number measures an even number, then it also measures half of it.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIX.23" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.31" } |>, "PropIX.31" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 31, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.31.md", "Statement" -> "If an odd number is relatively prime to any number, then it is also relatively prime to double it.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIX.28", "PropIX.30" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.32" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 32, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.32.md", "Statement" -> "Each of the numbers which are continually doubled beginning from a dyad is even-times-even only.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIX.13", "DefVII.6" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.33" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 33, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.33.md", "Statement" -> "If a number has its half odd, then it is even-times-odd only.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.6" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.34" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 34, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.34.md", "Statement" -> "If an [even] number neither is one of those which is continually doubled from a dyad, nor has its half odd, then it is both even-times-even and even-times-odd.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.6" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.35" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 35, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.35.md", "Statement" -> "If as many numbers as we please are in continued proportion, and there is subtracted from the second and the last numbers equal to the first, then the excess of the second is to the first as the excess of the last is to the sum of all those before it.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.11", "PropVII.13", "PropVII.12" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.36" } |>, "PropIX.36" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 36, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.36.md", "Statement" -> "If as many numbers as we please beginning from a unit are set out continuously in double proportion until the sum of all becomes prime, and if the sum multiplied into the last makes some number, then the product is perfect.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropVII.14", "PropVII.19", "PropIX.35", "PropIX.13", "DefVII.20", "PropVII.29", "PropVII.21", "PropVII.20", "DefVII.22" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.4" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 4, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.4.md", "Statement" -> "If a cubic number multiplied by a cubic number makes some number, then the product is a cube.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIX.3", "PropVII.17", "PropVIII.19", "PropVIII.8", "PropVIII.23" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.5" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 5, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.5.md", "Statement" -> "If a cubic number multiplied by any number makes a cubic number, then the multiplied number is also cubic.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIX.3", "PropVII.17", "PropVIII.19", "PropVIII.8", "PropVIII.23" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.6" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 6, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.6.md", "Statement" -> "If a number multiplied by itself makes a cubic number, then it itself is also cubic.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.20", "PropVIII.19", "PropVIII.8", "PropVIII.23" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.10" } |>, "PropIX.7" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 7, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.7.md", "Statement" -> "If a composite number multiplied by any number makes some number, then the product is solid.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.11", "DefVII.15", "DefVII.1" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "PropIX.8" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 8, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.8.md", "Statement" -> "If as many numbers as we please beginning from a unit are in continued proportion, then the third from the unit is square as are also those which successively leave out one, the fourth is cubic as are also all those which leave out two, and the seventh is at once cubic and square are also those which leave out five.", "Dependencies" -> { "DefVII.20", "PropVIII.22", "PropVIII.23" }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropIX.10", "PropIX.12", "PropIX.13", "PropIX.9" } |>, "PropIX.9" -> <| "Kind" -> "Prop", "Book" -> "IX", "Group" -> Null, "Num" -> 9, "File" -> "Wiki/BookIX/PropIX.9.md", "Statement" -> "If as many numbers as we please beginning from a unit are in continued proportion, and the number after the unit is square, then all the rest are also square; and if the number after the unit is cubic, then all the rest are also cubic.", "Dependencies" -> { "PropIX.8", "PropVIII.22", "PropIX.3", "PropVIII.23" }, "UsedIn" -> {  } |>, "DefX.I.1" -> <| "Kind" -> "Def", "Book" -> "X", "Group" -> "I", "Num" -> 1, "File" -> "Wiki/BookX/DefX.I.1.md", "Statement" -> "Those magnitudes are said to be *commensurable* which are measured by the same measure, and those *incommensurable* which cannot have any common measure.", "Dependencies" -> {  }, "UsedIn" -> { "PropX.113", "P